Topic-1: Architecture & Memory Management

Database Instance vs. Database Structure

SGA Components: Shared Pool, Buffer Cache, Redo Log Buffer, Large Pool, Java Pool

PGA Architecture: Private SQL Area, SQL Work Areas

Physical File Management: Datafiles, Control Files, Redo Log Files, Parameter Files (spfile / pfile)

Background Processes: DBWn, LGWR, CKPT, SMON, PMON, ARCn

Topic-2: Storage, Schema & Security
Storage Structure: Tablespaces, Segments, Extents, Data Blocks

ASM (Automatic Storage Management): Disk Groups, Redundancy, Striping

User Management: Roles, Privileges (System vs. Object), Profiles, Quotas

Database Security: Auditing, Data Redaction, TDE (Transparent Data Encryption)

Topic-3: Backup, Recovery & Data Transport
RMAN (Recovery Manager):

Full, Incremental (Level 0, Level 1), Cumulative Backups

Crosscheck, Delete Obsolete, Report/List Commands

Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR) & Disaster Recovery Scenarios

Data Transport Utilities:

Data Pump (expdp / impdp): Full, Schema, Table, Filter export/import

SQL*Loader & External Tables

Topic-4: High Availability & Scalability
Oracle Data Guard:

Physical vs. Logical Standby

Data Protection Modes (Maximum Performance, Availability, Protection)

Switchover vs. Failover Procedures, Active Data Guard

Oracle RAC (Real Application Clusters):

Multi-Node Cluster Architecture & Interconnect

Clusterware Services, OCR (Oracle Cluster Registry) & Voting Disk

Topic-5: Performance Tuning & Diagnostic
Performance Analysis Tools: AWR (Automatic Workload Repository), ADDM, ASH Reports

SQL Tuning: Execution Plans, Explain Plan, SQL Profiles, Indexing Strategies

Memory & I/O Tuning: SGA/PGA Advisory, Heavy Query Optimization, Lock & Blocking Session resolution

Topic-6: Maintenance, Patching & Infrastructure
Database Upgrades: Major Version Upgrades (e.g., 19c to 23c), DBUA vs. Manual Upgrade

Patch Management: OPatch utility, RU (Release Update) & RUR Application

Middleware & Networking: Listener (listener.ora), TNS (tnsnames.ora), WebLogic Managed Servers (WLS_FORMS/WLS_REPORTS), ORDS Integration

Automation: Linux Shell Scripting (Bash) for Cron Jobs, Health Checks, and Backup Automation